<interrogationes unitas="delineare">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I draw lines, rectangles and circles into a pixel buffer?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_creare_contextum tabula_pixelorum_creare_nuda fenestra_creare_tabulam_pixelorum delineare_rectangulum_plenum delineare_circulum">Make
      a TabulaPixelorum (fenestra_creare_tabulam_pixelorum for a window,
      tabula_pixelorum_creare_nuda without one), wrap it with
      delineare_creare_contextum(piscina, tabula), and call the
      primitives with a Color struct (color_ex_rgb), not a packed
      pixel. The RGB(...) macro in the header's example yields a packed
      i32 and does not fit the Color parameters. Nothing is shown until
      you present the table (fenestra_praesentare_pixela). Caution
      (audit 2026-10-18, unfixed): the outline delineare_rectangulum
      with altitudo 1 at y = 0 hangs, because its side edges run to
      y + altitudo - 2, which wraps to UINT_MAX in unsigned i32.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I pass negative coordinates, for a shape partly off the left or top edge?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_lineam delineare_lineam_horizontalem delineare_lineam_verticalem delineare_rectangulum_plenum delineare_circulum_plenum delineare_gradientum_radialem_dithered delineare_mandata" via="lib/delineare_mandata.worklog.md">Not
      safely. Coordinates are i32, which is unsigned, so -5 arrives as
      about 4e9. Outlines of circles and ellipses survive (off-table
      pixels are skipped). delineare_rectangulum_plenum silently drops
      the whole rectangle, visible part included, and the radial
      gradients draw nothing once the circle crosses the top or left
      edge. The rest can hang: delineare_lineam (so triangles and
      polygons) picks its direction with an unsigned compare and never
      reaches its end, and rectangle outlines and the other filled
      shapes draw through delineare_lineam_horizontalem or
      _verticalem, which loop from the smaller value up to the wrapped
      one - billions of steps, forever when an end is exactly -1. Clip
      to the table yourself, or emit Mandata and rasterize with
      delineare_mandata, which clips in signed space.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I restrict drawing to a rectangle (clipping)?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_ponere_praecisionem delineare_tollere_praecisionem delineare_vacare delineare_restituere_contextum">delineare_ponere_praecisionem(ctx,
      x, y, latitudo, altitudo) - x and y are s32 - and
      delineare_tollere_praecisionem to clear it. A negative x or y is
      raised to 0 but the width or height is NOT reduced by the same
      amount, so a clip at x = -5, width 10 covers columns 0 to 9 rather
      than 0 to 4. delineare_vacare ignores the clip and fills the whole
      table; delineare_restituere_contextum resets clip, mode and
      pattern.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I fill with a classic Mac pattern or draw in XOR mode?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_ponere_modum delineare_ponere_exemplar delineare_ponere_exemplar_internum delineare_ponere_offset_exemplaris exemplar_obtinere">Set
      MODUS_EXEMPLAR with delineare_ponere_modum, then the 8x8 bitmap
      with delineare_ponere_exemplar (8 bytes, one per row, high bit =
      leftmost pixel) or a built-in one with
      delineare_ponere_exemplar_internum (ids below EXEMPLAR_NUMERUS;
      others are ignored). Set bits get the colour, clear bits are left
      alone; the pattern is anchored at the offset from
      delineare_ponere_offset_exemplaris. MODUS_XOR XORs the whole
      packed pixel, alpha included, so XOR with an opaque colour over an
      opaque pixel leaves alpha 0.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I fill a rounded rectangle with delineare_rectangulum_rotundum_plenum and get the same footprint as a plain filled rectangle?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_rectangulum_rotundum_plenum delineare_rectangulum_rotundum delineare_rectangulum_plenum">No.
      With a radius above 0 it is meant to sit inside the border drawn
      by delineare_rectangulum_rotundum: the leftmost and rightmost
      columns stay empty, so draw the outline as well. With radius 0 it calls
      delineare_rectangulum_plenum and fills everything. The radius is
      capped at half the width and half the height.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I draw a dithered gradient limited to a palette?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_gradientum_linearem_dithered_cum_palette delineare_gradientum_radialem_dithered_cum_palette delineare_gradientum_linearem_dithered">The
      _cum_palette functions take an AlgorithusDithering and a Color
      array (NIHIL = pure black and white). They work in grey: both end
      colours and every palette entry are reduced to BT.601 luma, so a
      colour palette is matched by brightness only. The radial version
      always dithers with Bayer (8x8 when asked, otherwise 4x4), whatever
      algorithm you pass. The plain _dithered functions quantize each RGB
      channel to 0 or 255 with Floyd-Steinberg. Today only brightening
      gradients work: the shared interpolation runs in unsigned i32, so
      when the end value is below the start every pixel past the first
      clamps to full brightness. DITHERING_ATKINSON also drops its
      two-rows-down neighbour and spreads 5/8 of the error, not
      Atkinson's 6/8.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I draw gradients every frame without the context's piscina growing?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_gradientum_linearem_dithered delineare_creare_contextum piscina_notare piscina_reficere">Not
      on its own: the Floyd-Steinberg and Atkinson paths allocate their
      error rows from the piscina given to delineare_creare_contextum on
      every call and never release them. Bracket the drawing with
      piscina_notare and piscina_reficere on that piscina, or give the
      context a per-frame piscina. Bayer paths allocate
      nothing.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
